</addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IZUNO YUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAMADA AKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NARIYAMA KEIICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIHATA HIRONOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOMURA NORIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATABE YASUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEDA, KAZUSHIGE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IZUNO, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMADA, AKIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NARIYAMA, KEIICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIHATA, HIRONOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOMURA, NORIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATABE, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An egg candling method capable of detecting abnormal eggs highly accurately regardless of the size of eggs and a device used for the method. A normalizing unit divides a first signal received via a first band pass filter that passes wavelengths large in internal abnormality-caused absorption by a second signal received via a second band pass filter that passes wavelengths different in absorption according to the colors of egg shells, and divides a third signal received via a third band pass filter that passes wavelengths small in internal abnormality-caused absorption by the second signal to give the division results to a difference calculation unit. The difference calculation unit calculates the difference between the results for input to a decision unit, which compares the difference with a threshold value and, if the difference is larger, outputs a signal indicating an abnormal egg.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de mirage d'oeufs permettant de détecter les oeufs anormaux de façon très précise, indépendamment de la taille des oeufs, ainsi qu'un dispositif utilisé dans le cadre dudit procédé. Une unité de normalisation divise un premier signal reçu via un premier filtre passe-bande ne laissant passer que les longueurs d'onde à grande absorption causée par des anomalies internes par un deuxième signal reçu via un second filtre passe-bande ne faisant passer que les longueurs d'onde différentes en absorption selon la couleur des coquilles oeufs, et elle divise un troisième signal reçu via un troisième filtre passe-bande ne laissant passer que les longueurs d'onde à faible absorption causée par des anomalies internes par le deuxième signal en vue de la remise des résultats de la division à une unité de calcul de différence. Cette unité de calcul de différence calcule la différence entre les résultats destinés à être introduits dans une unité de décision, laquelle compare la différence avec une valeur de seuil et, si la différence dépasse cette valeur de seuil, produit en sortie un signal indiquant que l'oeuf est anormal.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>